  "subtitle": "The pocket computer that hides a thief and taunts you",
  "why_scout_cares": "Stop Thief (1979) contains one of the strangest computers of the era: a handheld Electronic Crime Scanner that secretly holds the location of an invisible thief, moves that thief adversarially through a city grid, and communicates everything through sound effects — footsteps, door creaks, breaking glass, subway rumbles. Players interrogate it with a Clue button, triangulate the thief's position by ear, and type an arrest code; the machine answers with a machine-gun burst and a siren, or a taunting 'na-na-na-na-na,' or a raspberry. A hidden-state electronic opponent with audio-only output, three years before Dark Tower, in every toy store in 1979.",
